-- Scheduled event: a field from the wrong Repeat must be rejected by `check`.
--
-- NEGATIVE TEST (.fail.mdl) — EXPECTED to fail `mxcli check`.
-- `make check-mdl` inverts the exit code for .fail.mdl files: an unexpected
-- pass would be reported as a regression of the MDL-SCHED01 rule.
--
-- The eight ScheduledEvents$*Schedule variants differ in WHICH fields they
-- carry, not just in their values. A DaySchedule has no Multiplier, so writing
-- one would put a property on the node that the type does not declare — the
-- shape that mxbuild accepts and Studio Pro cannot open
-- (System.InvalidOperationException at MprProperty).
--
-- The rule runs in the no-project pass, so a plain `mxcli check` catches it —
-- it is decidable from the statement alone, and exec calls the same function,
-- so check and exec cannot drift.
--
-- Correct form: drop Multiplier (Daily takes HourOfDay and MinuteOfHour), or
-- switch to a Repeat that has one.

create scheduled event Ops.Bad (
  Microflow: Ops.SE_Cleanup,
  Repeat: Daily,
  Multiplier: 3,
  HourOfDay: 4
);
